// Arm a configured channel.
//
// completes_when: CHn_CSR.en is set. The transfer is RUNNING, not finished.
// waits for:      nothing -- this is the arm half; wait_done() is the other.
//
// Setting `en` is also what clears the channel's `done` and `err` status
// (dma_regs_pkg), so a wait that follows this cannot observe the previous
// transfer's completion. That is the property the arm/wait split depends on,
// and it is why the model gives the device that behaviour rather than
// clear-on-read status.
//
// write_field() rather than a whole-register write: the configuration this is
// arming is already in the register and must survive. It is a read-modify-write
// on the bus (§21.14.1), which is safe here because nothing in this bank is
// clear-on-read.
import dma_regs_pkg::*;

extend component dma_c {

    target function void start_channel(int ch) {
        regs.ch_csr[ch].write_field("en", 1);
    }
}
